;; ...) cast around the constructed state, because method-set! checks its value
;; against the slot's declared (function none) typespec and a bare `state` does
;; not satisfy it. The decode's own (new 'static 'state :name ... :next ... :exit
;; ...) literal does not compile as written either: it keyword-inits :name/:next/
;; :exit, and jakx's own (deftype state ...) (goal_src/jakx/kernel/gkernel-h.gc)
;; declares only parent/code/trans/post/enter/event, six fields, with no :name or
;; :next at all (jak3's copy of the same deftype is identical - this is not a
;; jakx-only trim). So this uses state's own :methods (new ...) constructor
;; instead (the same positional form a697acd0a's stub already proved compiles),
